[Music]  in this video  we're going to walk through how to add  change or delete a billing account from  a google cloud project using the console  in order to perform these tasks you'll  need to be a project owner or project  billing manager on the project  and a billing account administrator or  billing account user for the target  billing account  get started by heading into the cloud  console you can start on any project  home page  then head to the navigation menu in the  left-hand pane choose billing  and then click manage billing accounts  you can also access the same destination  from the billing overview page by  expanding the drop-down list of billing  accounts  and clicking on manage billing accounts  select the my projects tab to view a  list of your projects  you'll also see the associated cloud  billing account for each project  if you have a project for which billing  is currently disabled you can re-enable  it by clicking on the three-dot menu  and selecting change billing in the drop  down  choose the desired billing account and  click set account  you can also change the billing account  currently attached to a project  following a similar process  identify the project and click the three  dot menu and select  change billing in the drop down choose  the desired destination billing account  and click  set account if you would like to remove  a billing account from a project or in  other words  disable billing identify the project and  click the three dot menu  then select disable billing you'll be  asked to confirm that you want to  disable billing for this project  a quick word of caution disabling  billing on a project might cause some  resources to be removed  and become non-recoverable when you are  ready click disable billing  if at any time the options to change  billing or disable billing are not  available to you  this means you may not have the  permissions needed to make this change  in that case be sure to review the  permissions requirements shared at the  beginning of this video  head over to the documentation to check  out more details  you

